{"name":"Stone Creek","hex":"#8f9183","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"creek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small inlet, often saltwater, leading to the sea or to the main channel of a river, especially a river estuary.","The inner part of a port that is used as a dock for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stony Creek (Sacramento River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Stony Creek is a 73.5-mile (118.3 km)-long tributary of the Sacramento River in Northern California. It drains a watershed of more than 700 square miles (1,800 km2) on the west side of the Sacramento Valley in Glenn, Colusa, Lake and Tehama Counties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Stony_Gorge_Dam.jpg/330px-Stony_Gorge_Dam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stony_Creek_(Sacramento_River_tributary)"},{"title":"Holland Brook","blocks":[{"text":"Holland Brook is a tributary of the South Branch Raritan River in Hunterdon and Somerset Counties, New Jersey in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Holland_Brook2.JPG/330px-Holland_Brook2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holland_Brook"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg/500px-Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg/1280px-Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg/500px-Black_Butte_Lake_%286166037573%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black Butte Lake is the largest impoundment of Stony Creek and is the boundary between the upper and lower parts of the watershed.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Butte_Lake_(6166037573).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Appendix_to_the_Journals_of_the_Senate_and_Assembly_of_the_session_of_the_Legislature_of_the_State_of_California_%281917%29_%2814597482258%29.jpg/500px-Appendix_to_the_Journals_of_the_Senate_and_Assembly_of_the_session_of_the_Legislature_of_the_State_of_California_%281917%29_%2814597482258%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org